摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"TypeScript runtime for LLM agent graphs with bounded loops, live updates, isolated Git worktrees, and explicit integration. Framework-agnostic core, OpenAI-compatible runner, and plugins for Pi and DeepSeek Harness.","id":"gh:1369351986","install_available":false,"language":"TypeScript","name":"braid","slug":"Epsirom/braid","topics":["agent-orchestration","agent-runtime","ai-agents","bounded-loops","dsh-plugin","git-worktree","graph-execution","llm","multi-agent","nodejs","openai-compatible","parallel-execution","pi-package","typescript"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"TypeScript runtime for LLM agent graphs with bounded loops, live updates, isolated Git worktrees, an"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"d explicit integration. Framework-agnostic core, OpenAI-compatible runner, and plugins for Pi and De"},{"id":"p1s3","text":"gration. Framework-agnostic core, OpenAI-compatible runner, and plugins for Pi and DeepSeek Harness."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# Braid"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"Braid coordinates multiple LLM agents as a graph. Define each agent's task and\nwhich results it need"},{"id":"p3s2","text":"s; Braid runs independent tasks in parallel and passes\ntheir outputs to the next step."},{"id":"p4s1","text":"Use it as a TypeScript/JavaScript library or as a plugin for Pi or DeepSeek Harness."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"## Why Braid?"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"For a code review, one agent can check correctness while another checks test\ncoverage. A third waits"},{"id":"p6s2","text":" for both results and writes the final review:"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"Each box is a task (a **node**); each arrow passes a result to a dependent task\n(an **edge**). Braid"},{"id":"p8s2","text":" manages when tasks run and gives each agent its own context.\nFor agents that edit code, it also pro"},{"id":"p8s3","text":"vides separate Git worktrees; an explicit\n`integrate` task applies selected changes to your checkout"},{"id":"p8s4","text":"ides separate Git worktrees; an explicit\n`integrate` task applies selected changes to your checkout."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"Graphs can also branch on a choice an agent makes, repeat work in a cycle until a\nchoice ends it, an"},{"id":"p9s2","text":"d be edited, rerun, or paused while running. See runnable examples\nand execution control when you ne"},{"id":"p9s3","text":", or paused while running. See runnable examples\nand execution control when you need those features."},{"id":"p10s1","text":"## Get started"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"| Where you want to use Braid | Start here |"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"| In your own application | Install `@chrok/braid` and supply a model runner |\n| In Pi | Install `@c"},{"id":"p12s2","text":"hrok/pi-braid` for background agents and a live panel; `pi -p \"task\"` waits for background jobs in C"},{"id":"p12s3","text":"I |\n| In DeepSeek Harness | Install `@chrok/dsh-braid` for background agents and a native Web graph "},{"id":"p12s4","text":"n DeepSeek Harness | Install `@chrok/dsh-braid` for background agents and a native Web graph panel |"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"## Install in your application"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"Requires Node.js 22+ and ESM imports. The core has no runtime dependencies."},{"id":"p15s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"Save this as `example.mjs` and run `node example.mjs` (no API key needed):"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"For a live provider, use the adapter in the API example below. Installation and\nrunning the example "},{"id":"p18s2","text":"above do not make model requests. In a Git checkout, Braid\ncreates a fresh worktree for each executi"},{"id":"p18s3","text":"on. Only explicit `integrate` nodes\nwrite results back to the source checkout. Read workspace behavi"},{"id":"p18s4","text":"or\nbefore running a custom adapter against a repository."},{"id":"p19s1","text":"## Install in Pi"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"With Pi 1.2.0 and Node.js 22.19+:"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"Run `/reload` and ask Pi to analyze a task with Braid. Background progress appears\nautomatically abo"},{"id":"p22s2","text":"ve the input editor; open `/braid` for the full live panel.\nUse `/braid:review [target or focus]` fo"},{"id":"p22s3","text":"r a bounded parallel review/fix loop\n(at most three review rounds), and `/braid:clear` to clear the "},{"id":"p22s4","text":"progress widget\n(run it again to restore it).\nnpm installs the exact matching core dependency; no ch"},{"id":"p22s5","text":"eckout is needed\nfor published versions. To try the current source checkout, follow the\nlocal Pi ins"},{"id":"p22s6","text":"\nfor published versions. To try the current source checkout, follow the\nlocal Pi installation guide."},{"id":"p23s1","text":"This snapshot uses the actual panel renderer and fake responses. See the\nPi guide for background job"},{"id":"p23s2","text":"s, cancellation, and local\ninstallation, and compatibility for the tested versions."},{"id":"p24s1","text":"## Install in DeepSeek Harness"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"Requires Node.js 22.19+ and DeepSeek Harness 0.2.0-rc.2, the pinned developer-preview\nhost version. "},{"id":"p25s2","text":"DSH support starts with Braid 0.3.1; the npm badge shows availability."},{"id":"p26s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"Restart the profile, ask DSH to run a task with Braid, and open **Braid** in the\nsession header or r"},{"id":"p27s2","text":"ight sidebar. Use your own profile name in place of `web`.\nnpm installs the matching core dependency"},{"id":"p27s3","text":" automatically. See the\nDSH guide for tools, live controls, the Web panel,\nand installation from a l"},{"id":"p27s4","text":". See the\nDSH guide for tools, live controls, the Web panel,\nand installation from a local checkout."},{"id":"p28s1","text":"## API"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"After installing the package, submit the graph in one call;\nconfiguration and the trusted provider a"},{"id":"p29s2","text":"dapter are separate from the graph data:"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"The detailed route starts `benefits` and `risks` concurrently. The brief route\nskips both, propagate"},{"id":"p31s2","text":"s their inactivity, and runs `answer` with only `route`'s\noutput. The graph has no special fork, bra"},{"id":"p31s3","text":" and runs `answer` with only `route`'s\noutput. The graph has no special fork, branch, or join nodes."},{"id":"p32s1","text":"## Internal architecture and scope"},{"id":"p33s1","text":"- `src/types.ts`: public graph, provider, and result types.\n- `src/validate.ts`: strict validation, "},{"id":"p33s2","text":"graph snapshot,\ndependency indexes, and iterative validation of acyclic regions and cycles.\n- `src/r"},{"id":"p33s3","text":"untime.ts`: lineages of execution instances, edge resolution, explicit state transitions,\nbounded co"},{"id":"p33s4","text":"ncurrent scheduling, invocation deadlines, execution events, and result accounting.\n- `src/workspace"},{"id":"p33s5","text":"s.ts`: Git snapshots, checkpoint refs, merge\nserialization, local Git tools, and worktree cleanup.\n-"},{"id":"p33s6","text":" `src/adapters/openai.ts`: optional provider translation.\n- `integrations/dsh/`: native DeepSeek Har"},{"id":"p33s7","text":"ness model/tool adapter, agent-scoped jobs, reminders, and a native Web graph panel.\n- `integrations"},{"id":"p33s8","text":"/pi/`: thin Pi model-registry/tool adapter, Mermaid graph renderer, and live execution renderer (`di"},{"id":"p33s9","text":"splay.ts`).\n- `test/`: deterministic scheduling, execution-event, and intercepted HTTP/tool tests."},{"id":"p34s1","text":"There is one in-memory execution context per run, plus a process-local mutex\nper source checkout for"},{"id":"p34s2","text":" integrate agents. Worktree registration and removal are\nserialized per common Git directory within "},{"id":"p34s3","text":"the process; model calls remain\nconcurrent. These locks do not coordinate other processes. `rootRunI"},{"id":"p34s4","text":"d` equals\n`runId`. Centralized invocation admission and\nusage aggregation leave places to thread a s"},{"id":"p34s5","text":"hared root budget in a future\nnested-run implementation; **nested runs and shared budget enforcement"},{"id":"p34s6","text":" are not\nimplemented**. The current scheduler deliberately rescans a small graph after\ncompletions; "},{"id":"p34s7","text":"`onEvent` is an observer for diagnostics and visualization, not a\nscheduler event bus."},{"id":"p35s1","text":"Out of scope: arbitrary\ncode nodes, durable workflow recovery, saved templates, a graphical editing "},{"id":"p35s2","text":"UI,\nand recursive Braid calls from model nodes. The RSI Mode and Zen Mode milestones\nrevisit some of"},{"id":"p35s3","text":" these boundaries; see ROADMAP.md."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
